  "results": [
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1",
      "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 0.5,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "wizards' college": "synthesis_gap",
        "arcane lockdown": "hit",
        "wards": "hit",
        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a **city-wide arcane lockdown/purification measure**, but the catch is it would affect the entire population and risk isolating parts of the city, potentially harming or trapping civilians without proper protections.\n\nEvidence:\n- the city (defenses): \u201cProposed arcane lockdown\u201d\n- the city (geography): \u201cEntire city is within purification scope\u201d\n- the city (operational_status): \u201cAt risk of having parts isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed\u201d\n- the city (governance): \u201cCouncil is choosing a plan for handling city citizens in relation to the tainted meat issue\u201d\n- Players (role): \u201cMay be called upon to help set up or maintain magical wards\u201d\n- Players (defenses): \u201cIf players do not have the amulets, traps may target them.\u201d\n\nAnalysis:\nThe projection never explicitly states \u201cthe wizards say X,\u201d but the only plan matching an emergency, wizard-led response is the **arcane lockdown/purification**. The \u201ccatch\u201d emerges from its side effects: it\u2019s indiscriminate (city-wide), could **seal or isolate districts**, and relies on **magical defenses/amulets**, meaning unprotected citizens (or players) could be harmed or restricted.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster",
      "question": "Who's actually in the council chamber for the Session 12 fight with the Wolf?",
