      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards; he\u2019s aggressively anti-cult, pushing magical detection and even a citywide lockdown to root out their influence.\n\nEvidence:\n- Headmaster Tinkerbright: \u201cRepresentative of the Arcane\u201d and head of the Wizard\u2019s College (OBSERVED role, CANON faction)\n- Headmaster Tinkerbright: \u201cWill be first to present his plan\u201d at the council (OBSERVED goals)\n- Headmaster Tinkerbright: \u201cPlans to magically lock the city down\u201d and \u201cuse a rune to find corrupted meat\u201d (OBSERVED goals)\n- Headmaster Tinkerbright: \u201cEager to deploy Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence\u201d (OBSERVED goals)\n- Headmaster Tinkerbright: \u201cTakes any threat to the city seriously\u201d and views the corrupted meat as \u201ca perversion of magic\u201d (CANON loyalty/alignment)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Representative of the Arcane; Head of the Wizard\u2019s College  \n- Faction: Wizard\u2019s College  \n- Goals: Magical lockdown; detection runes; mobilize arcane resources  \n- Alignment/Angle: Sees the cult\u2019s magic as a perversion; treats them as a serious existential threat",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
