        "killing blow": "hit",
        "bonogo": "hit",
        "decapitated": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014specifically \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\u2014despite earlier escape attempts while invisible.\n\nEvidence:\n- the Wolf (physical_condition, OBSERVED): \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\n- ent_bonogo (role, OBSERVED): \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it\u201d\n- the Wolf (operational_status, OBSERVED): \u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible\u201d; \u201cescapes\u201d; \u201crushes by Bonogo and attempts to disengage to run\u201d\n- the Wolf (physical_condition, OBSERVED): \u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d; \u201cInvisible\u201d\n\nAnalysis:\nThere is a clear conflict between the Wolf escaping (invisibility + fleeing via secret passage) and the terminal outcome. The decapitation is a terminal state and is reinforced by Bonogo physically removing the head, so it supersedes the earlier escape facts. The most current state is that the Wolf is dead, with the body separated and the head taken. Earlier \u201cescapes\u201d describe a moment during the fight, not the final outcome.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: Dead (\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d)\n- Final Handler: ent_bonogo transported the head\n- Tactics Used: Invisibility, illusion duplicates, escape attempt via secret passage\n- Role: Central adversary in council chamber battle",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
