      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence Thalia is corrupted like the guards; what\u2019s shown points to her being influenced or commanded by the Wolf instead, which is a different mechanism.\n\nEvidence:\n- the Wolf: \u201corders Thalia to attack the group.\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Guards: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes.\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- the Wolf: \u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- Guards: corruption is tied to \u201ccorrupted meat\u201d and grants effects like temporary HP (CANON)\n\nAnalysis:\nThe guards\u2019 corruption is clearly marked by the oily sheen and linked to the tainted meat system. Thalia is never described with that condition in the provided context. Instead, her aggression is directly tied to the Wolf issuing commands, suggesting control, coercion, or manipulation rather than the same corruption affecting the guards. Without explicit mention of the oily sheen or meat-based effects on Thalia, these should be treated as different phenomena.",
