      "answer": "TL;DR: The council chamber actively interferes with the fight via arcane traps, environmental hazards like falling debris, and disorienting magical effects\u2014especially punishing anyone without the proper amulets.\n\nEvidence:\n- Players: \u201cCan be temporarily paralyzed by arcane trap bursts\u201d and \u201cCan take 2d6 force damage from arcane trap bursts\u201d (OBSERVED, Players physical_condition)\n- Players: \u201cForced to dodge falling debris hazards\u201d (OBSERVED, Players physical_condition)\n- Players: \u201cIf players do not have the amulets, traps may target them\u201d (CANON, Players defenses)\n- Guards: \u201cGuards are exempt from arcane trap targeting\u201d and \u201ctrusted guards wear amulets\u201d (CANON, Guards relationship_tags)\n- Players: \u201cDisoriented by the illusory walls/illusion spells\u201d (CANON, Players mental_state)\n- Guards: \u201cAlerted by Rune alarms\u201d (OBSERVED, Guards operational_status)\n- Players: \u201cPlayers might notice an unusual change in the hum when something significant happens\u201d (CANON, Players portrayal_notes)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane trap system keyed to amulets\n- Hazards:\n  - Arcane trap bursts (paralysis + 2d6 force damage)\n  - Falling debris\n  - Illusory walls / disorientation effects\n  - Rune alarm triggers (escalation mechanic)\n- Environmental cues: Shifting hum signaling trap or system changes",
