      "answer": "TL;DR: There isn\u2019t enough evidence in the projection to determine whether Thalia is trustworthy; however, there are indirect signs that something may be off around her.\n\nEvidence:\n- Stafl: \u201cAttacks Thalia after being revived\u201d (OBSERVED) \u2014 suggests Thalia may have been perceived as a threat or target in that moment.\n- Caelynn: \u201cInstructs Thalia to bring a potion to Lesandra at the Wizard\u2019s College\u201d (OBSERVED) \u2014 indicates at least some level of operational trust from Caelynn.\n- Guards: \u201cAll checked guards have an oily sheen to their eyes\u201d and corruption is spreading (OBSERVED) \u2014 establishes a broader context where individuals may be compromised.\n\nAnalysis:\nNo direct facts describe Thalia\u2019s behavior, mental state, or allegiance. The mixed signals\u2014being trusted with a task by Caelynn but attacked by Stafl\u2014could reflect confusion, charm effects, or misidentification rather than clear guilt. The wider corruption threat (e.g., oily-eyed guards) means suspicion is reasonable, but not confirmed.",
