      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room should feel tense and recently chaotic\u2014guards shaken and on alert, signs of illusion magic and disruption lingering, and the Wolf\u2019s **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** state with his **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d** standing out as a key, unsettling detail.\n\nEvidence:\n- the Wolf (physical_condition): \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d; \u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d\n- the Wolf (defenses): Creates illusory duplicates, implying visual confusion/disruption in the room\n- Guards (current_location): \u201cGuards are placed in a ring along the wall.\u201d\n- Guards (mental_state): \u201cLooking tense\u201d; \u201cvisibly tense\u201d; \u201cIn disbelief\u201d\n- Guards (operational_status): \u201cAlerted by Rune alarms and actively stopping people outside Council Chambers\u201d\n- Players (physical_condition): \u201cForced to dodge falling debris hazards\u201d; \u201cCan be temporarily paralyzed by arcane trap bursts\u201d\n- the Wolf (goals): \u201csecret escape tunnel beneath the council chamber\u201d\n- Players (portrayal_notes): \u201cPlayers might notice an unusual change in the hum when something significant happens.\u201d\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps (burst damage, paralysis), rune alarms active\n- Environment: Evidence of illusion magic and possible debris from hazards\n- NPC State: Guards forming a perimeter, tense and reacting\n- Notable Feature: Secret escape tunnel beneath the chamber\n- Sensory Detail: Subtle change in the city\u2019s ambient hum indicating something significant occurred",
