      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead\u2014he was \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\u2014and he showed clear signs of corruption (e.g., \u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d) prior to death.\n\nEvidence:\n- the Wolf (physical_condition, OBSERVED): \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\n- ent_bonogo (role, OBSERVED): \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it\u201d\n- the Wolf (physical_condition, OBSERVED): \u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d\n- the Wolf (mental_state, OBSERVED): \u201cbegging to be killed; desperate; feels regret\u201d\n- the Wolf (operational_status, OBSERVED): earlier \u201cescapes\u201d and invisibility attempts (pre-terminal state)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: Dead (\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d)\n- Corruption: Present prior to death (\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d)\n- Faction: Cultist\n- Role: Saboteur; adversary in council chamber battle\n- Rank: second-in-command of the guard\n\nAnalysis:\nAlthough the Wolf previously escaped and acted while invisible, the later terminal outcome (\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d) is the final and overriding state from OBSERVED play. His corruption is confirmed before death, but no evidence indicates it was resolved.",
