      "answer": "TL;DR: Thalia was **not corrupted**; she was **ensorcelled (magically influenced) by the Wolf**, meaning she was being played rather than willingly complicit. This ties directly to the Wolf\u2019s role as a corrupting, deceptive influence controlling others.\n\nEvidence:\n- Thalia: \u201censorcelled by the Wolf\u201d and \u201censorcelled (unbeknownst to her)\u201d (OBSERVED, Thalia physical_condition)\n- Thalia: \u201cCharmed status ended\u201d and later \u201cRealizes how dire the situation truly is\u201d and \u201cInnocent\u201d (OBSERVED, Thalia mental_state)\n- Thalia: \u201cdoes not have an oily sheen to her eyes.\u201d (OBSERVED, Thalia physical_condition)\n- Guards: corruption is associated with \u201coily sheen to their eyes.\u201d (OBSERVED, Guards physical_condition)\n- Thalia: \u201coverlooks corruption within the guard due to ensorcellment\u201d (CANON, Thalia portrayal_notes)\n- Wolf: \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d (OBSERVED, the Wolf goals)\n- Wolf: tagged as \u201ccorrupting_influence\u201d and uses deception/manipulation (CANON/OBSERVED, the Wolf role/goals)\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia (status): Enscorcelled, not physically corrupted\n- Corruption marker: Oily sheen in eyes (absent in Thalia)\n- Wolf (role): Manipulator, cultist, corrupting influence\n- Control method: Enchantment/charm rather than physical corruption\n\nAnalysis:\nThe distinction is clear in-world: **corruption = oily eyes + physical influence**, while **Thalia lacks that marker and instead was magically controlled**. Once the charm breaks, her perspective shifts, reinforcing that she was being used by the Wolf rather than acting of her own will.",
